##
A project that lists two programs.

Program is declared once in a compilation, because it is the name the entry point lives
in. Two files each declaring one cannot be built together, and the second is named.

The folder rule never runs into this, since it takes only the program that was named and
the shared code beside it. A project has to be told.
##

project TwoPrograms
    source ../runtime/divide-by-zero.pc
    source ../runtime/index-out-of-range.pc
end project
